er-html/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order-svg: Generate a standalone textbook-style stroke-order SVG for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke — completed strokes in black, current stroke highlighted with red number and directional arrow, remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill when the user wants ONLY the stroke-order diagram as a raw SVG (no HTML wrapper, no metadata). For the full HTML kanji study sheet with ON/KUN/mnemonic/examples bundled in, use the sibling skill `kanji-stroke-order-html` instead. (file: r0/kanji-stroke-order-svg/SKILL.md)\n- masterclass-builder: Use this skill to design rigorous, deep masterclasses and multi-module curricula (roughly 90 minutes per module, extensible to 15-20h) that build durable understanding and autonomous capability, not passive \"AI slop.\" Trigger this whenever the user wants to create a masterclass, a course, a deep curriculum, a structured learning program, progressive exercises on a topic, a study plan, or wants to genuinely LEARN a domain (not just get a one-shot answer), even if they do not use the word \"course.\" Covers learner profiling, 80/20 syllabus design, mechanism-level explanation (why before how), scaffolded progressive exercises, active recall, decision-f (file: r0/masterclass-builder/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-knowledge-capture: Capture conversations and decisions into structured Notion pages; use when turning chats/notes into wiki entries, how-tos, decisions, or FAQs with proper linking. (file: r7/notion-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-meeting-intelligence: Prepare meeting materials with Notion context and supplemental research; use when gathering context, drafting agendas/pre-reads, and tailoring materials to attendees. (file: r7/notion-meeting-intelligence/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-research-documentation: Research across Notion and synthesize into structured documentation; use when gathering info from multiple Notion sources to produce briefs, comparisons, or reports with citations. (file: r7/notion-research-documentation/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-spec-to-implementation: Turn Notion specs into implementation plans, tasks, and progress tracking; use when implementing PRDs/feature specs and creating Notion plans + tasks from them. (file: r7/notion-spec-to-implementation/SKILL.md)\n- pdf:pdf: Read, create, inspect, render, and verify PDF files where visual layout matters. Use Poppler rendering plus Python tools such as reportlab, pdfplumber, and pypdf for generation and extraction. (file: r8/pdf/26.709.11516/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Create or edit PowerPoint or Google Slides decks (file: r8/presentations/26.709.11516/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- reduce-echo: Répare un enregistrement audio/vidéo (appel, interview, visio) qui souffre d'écho ou de réverbération causés par une double capture audio — typiquement un micro qui recapte le son sorti des enceintes, ou deux chemins audio mixés dans la même piste avec un délai qui DÉRIVE dans le temps (ex 30ms au début, 50ms une heure plus tard). Chaîne complète en plusieurs passes IA + DSP, jamais une seule : filtre soustractif adaptatif par blocs (mesure et suit le délai qui dérive), VoiceFixer (régénération générative de la voix, efface l'écho qu'un simple filtre ne peut pas), réparation automatique des passages que les modèles génératifs avalent/gatent (fui (file: r0/reduce-echo/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-building: Use Sites to build websites, including landing pages, portfolios, dashboards, portals, trackers, hubs, and internal tools. Always use Sites when the project contains `.openai/hosting.json`. (file: r3/sites-building/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-hosting: Host websites with Sites. Always use after `sites-building`, and use for website publishing, deployment, hosting management, or projects containing `.openai/hosting.json`. (file: r3/sites-hosting/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Create, edit, analyze, and