pact surface (existing state, conflicts, limits and deadlines, security/legal, partial failure, backward compatibility, scale, recurring cost, observability, edge cases, checks, reversibility), runs a domain-specific premortem, then del (file: r0/think-of-everything/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools in conversation. Use when asked to show how something works, make simulators or labs, maps, plots, charts or graphs, comparisons, scenarios, adjustable inputs, and exploration. (file: r2/visualize/1.0.11/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- ytb-dlp: Télécharger des vidéos, pistes audio, sous-titres ou métadonnées depuis YouTube et les nombreux sites pris en charge par yt-dlp. Utiliser quand l'utilisateur demande une commande yt-dlp, un téléchargement média, une sélection de formats, une extraction audio ou le diagnostic d'un téléchargement yt-dlp. (file: r0/ytb-dlp/SKILL.md)\n- zenray-backup-mirror: Déclencher, monitorer ou arrêter le second système de backup ZenRayProgress (scripts/backup-mirror.mjs — miroir froid indépendant, second exemplaire des binaires ZenRayShards sur des repos privés séparés). Déclencheurs — \"lance le backup\", \"vérifie le second backup\", \"sauvegarde en double tel dossier\", \"où en est le backup-mirror\", \"monitore le backup\". JAMAIS lancer le run complet sans confirmation explicite de Matthieu — toujours proposer --dry-run --limit=N en premier. (file: r0/zenray-backup-mirror/SKILL.md)\n- zenray-git-bulk-safety: Safely repair, migrate, reindex, or bulk-upload ZenRayProgress media and manifests with Git transport instead of GitHub REST/raw requests. Use for thumbnail rollouts, shard migrations, bulk manifest changes, re-ingestion, or any operation touching more than a few GitHub files. (file: r0/zenray-git-bulk-safety/SKILL.md)\n- zenrayshards-upload-media: Skill UNIQUE d'upload média ZenRayProgress — détecte automatiquement l'entrée et route vers le bon pipeline. FICHIERS LOCAUX (vidéo/image, mélangés OK) vers ZenRayShards v2 (vid=privé+chiffré+hvc1, img=public jsDelivr) ; LIEN YouTube vers nœud .media.json type:'youtube' ou audioOnly:true. Pour cent fichiers ou plus, réparation, migration, réindexation ou modification de manifestes, impose d'abord zenray-git-bulk-safety : clone/pull/commit/push Git, jamais REST/raw dans une boucle. Déclencheurs — upload zenrayshards, upload vid zenrayshards, uploade ce(s) fichier(s)/cette vidéo/cette musique, tout chemin local ou lien youtube.com/youtu.be avec inte (file: r0/zenrayshards-upload-media/SKILL.md)\n</skills_instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<apps_instructions>\n## Apps (Connectors)\nApps (Connectors) can be explicitly triggered in user messages in the format `[$app-name](app://{connector_id})`. Apps can also be implicitly triggered as long as the context suggests usage of available apps.\nAn app is equivalent to a set of MCP tools within the `codex_apps` MCP.\nAn installed app's MCP tools are either provided to you already, or can be lazy-loaded through the `tool_search` tool. If `tool_search` is available, the apps that are searchable by `tools_search` will be listed by it.\nDo not additionally call list_mcp_resources or list_mcp_resource_templates for apps.\n</apps_instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<plugins_instructions>\n## Plugins\nA plugin is a local bundle of skills, MCP servers, and apps.\n### How to use plugins\n- Skill naming: If a plugin contributes skills, those skill entries are prefixed with `plugin_name:` in the Skills list.\n- MCP naming: Plugin-provided MCP tools keep standard MCP identifiers such as `mcp__server__tool`; use tool provenance to tell which plugin they come from.\n- Trigger rules: If the user explicitly names a plugin, prefer capabilities associated with that plugin for that turn.\n- Relationship to capabilities: Plugins are not invoked directly. Use their underlying skills, MCP tools, and app tools to help solve the task.\n- Relevance: Determine what a plugin can h