{"timestamp":"2026-07-13T09:36:29.092Z","ordinal":149,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019f5ad5-ca26-71c3-b09f-a7a101244e43","turn_id":"019f5a81-0017-7cc1-9926-1478d912b904","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-6f629a49-66e8-423a-8684-de16e5fa178e","changes":{"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory/_TEMP/hatch-pet-runs/clawd-coder-c-20260713/qa/look-mechanics.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Clawd Coder — look mechanics\n\n## Stable construction\n\nClawd is a low, wide orange pixel alien/octopus whose four short straight legs stay planted on one shared baseline. Its compact dark MacBook remains attached in front of the lower torso: screen, hinge, narrow keyboard deck, and trackpad do not change size, detach, or drift. The two simple side manipulators stay attached to the body and remain plausibly aligned with the keyboard. The face is a flat orange surface with two tiny black square printed eyes, not separate physical eyeballs.\n\n## Natural looking motion\n\nThe lower body, legs, laptop hinge, and keyboard anchor remain fixed. Gaze is expressed by a restrained turn of the face plane and upper body, a one- or two-logical-pixel migration/redraw of the square-eye features within that face plane, and a matching change in the single terracotta side facet. The small laptop follows the torso only through a subtle, continuous side-on foreshortening; it must never rotate as a whole sprite or become dominant. Manipulators shift minimally along the keyboard and may lag one logical pixel after the upper body, while remaining connected.\n\n## Cardinal pose families\n\n- **000 / up:** eyes rise visibly toward the top face edge; the top orange plane is fractionally more exposed and the screen remains front-attached. The body does not lift off its baseline.\n- **090 / screen-right:** the right orange side facet is visibly exposed; both eye marks and the upper face plane shift toward the viewer's right. The right end of the MacBook is subtly more side-on, without moving its base.\n- **180 / down:** eyes sit noticeably lower toward the MacBook/keyboard; the top plane recedes and both manipulators settle fractionally down toward the keys. No laptop enlargement.\n- **270 / screen-left:** the left orange side facet is visibly exposed; face features and the upper plane shift toward the viewer's left. The left end of the MacBook is subtly more side-on, with continuous unchanged baseline.\n\n## Motion budget and order\n\nEach 22.5-degree step advances the face plane, eyes, facet, and tiny keyboard-hand offset by approximately the same small visual amount. Direction order is a continuous clockwise loop: `000 -> 022.5 -> 045 -> 067.5 -> 090 -> 112.5 -> 135 -> 157.5 -> 180 -> 202.5 -> 225 -> 247.5 -> 270 -> 292.5 -> 315 -> 337.5 -> 000`. Do not use whole-sprite rotation, whole-cell rotation, affine skew, replacement eyes, labels, degree marks, shadows, detached effects, scenery, or new props.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory/_TEMP/hatch-pet-runs/clawd-coder-c-20260713/qa/look-mechanics.md\n"},"completed_at_ms":1783935389092}}
